From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:27:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77759: stay online while a full battery is
 on the charger

charger_input_valid() required both CHGIN_OK and CHG_OK in CHG_INT_OK.
CHG_OK clears when the charge is done: on a Pixel 7 Pro on a laptop port,
CHG_INT_OK went from 0xdd to 0xcd as CHG_DETAILS_01 reached DONE (0x4),
and online and present dropped to 0 with the cable in and the mode still
CHG_BUCK_ON. Userspace then counts a full phone on the charger as running
on battery (upower applies its battery policy).

Report the input from CHGIN_OK alone; the status property already says
Full, and charger faults through status and health.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
index 7764ac15d..61e118fd9 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
@@ -158,8 +158,12 @@ static int charger_input_valid(struct max77759_charger *chg)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	return (val & MAX77759_CHGR_REG_CHG_INT_CHG) &&
-		(val & MAX77759_CHGR_REG_CHG_INT_CHGIN);
+	/*
+	 * CHGIN alone says whether the input is there. CHG_OK clears when a
+	 * charge is done (and on charger faults), which the status property
+	 * already reports.
+	 */
+	return !!(val & MAX77759_CHGR_REG_CHG_INT_CHGIN);
 }
 
 static int get_online(struct max77759_charger *chg)
